              time  can  be given in free format.  The time zone LLTT stands for
              local time; other common time zone names  are  understood.   For
              example,  the  following  _d_a_t_es  are equivalent if local time is
              January 11, 1990, 8pm Pacific Standard Time, eight hours west of
              Coordinated Universal Time (UTC):

